          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            6. Protein per Serving and Cost per 25 g
          </h2>

          <p>
            Price per tub tells you almost nothing. Plant powders range from about 20 g to 30 g of protein per serving, and servings per container vary widely, so two tubs at the same shelf price can differ in real value by half. The number that matters is cost per 25 g of protein: divide the price by the number of servings, divide again by the grams of protein per serving, then multiply by 25. Run that sum once and the cheap-looking tubs often stop looking cheap.
          </p>

          <p>
            On our list, the unflavored single-ingredient pea powders, Naked Pea and NOW Sports Pea Protein, sit in the budget tier at typical retail prices. Orgain Organic Protein looks inexpensive per tub, but at about 21 g of protein per two-scoop serving its cost per 25 g lands in the middle. Garden of Life Sport and Vega Sport sit in the mid-to-premium tier, where you are paying for certification and a full 30 g dose. Momentous is a premium product and priced like one.
          </p>

          <p>
            Protein per calorie matters if you are cutting. A clean pea isolate like Naked Pea gives about 27 g of protein in roughly 120 calories, close to 22 g of protein per 100 calories. Orgain gives about 21 g in roughly 150 calories, nearer 14 g per 100 calories, because its formula includes fiber, gums and other ingredients that add calories without adding protein. Neither is wrong, but they are not the same product.
          </p>

          <p>
            Remember the leucine adjustment too. If you need 1.5 servings of a 20 g product to match one 30 g serving of another, its effective cost per shake is 50% higher than the label suggests. Buying the largest tub you will finish before it goes stale, and using subscribe-and-save discounts, cuts cost per gram meaningfully. Just do not let cost per 25 g override testing; the cheapest gram of protein is not a bargain if you have no idea what else is in the tub.
          </p>

